ck is under the account's BedrockDailySpendCapDeny explicit deny (attached to rebar-gerrit-instance-role), so any production plan review would degrade to INDETERMINATE. The deny lifts at 00:00 UTC (16:00 PST).\n- Next: once mite closes and the cap has lifted, run review-plan on this ticket, claim it, then do the two review_plan_start runs through production MCP and record them on the epic.","timestamp":1794493666051655644},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress 2026-11-12 14:22 PST: plan review r2 PASS (Anthropic path, 14:07-14:19 PST). Claimed. Advisory adopted: a redo of the pipeline run (deploy SHA change, or a retry) would hit idempotent reuse once any engine has signed a current attestation, and agents may not pass force. So a redo first makes a material edit to the target ticket (one sentence added to its Context); that stales the attestation and makes both runs review afresh. The target mindless-misogynic-nematode now has a full plan and file_impact. Local unsigned pre-checks under both engines are running now; the production runs wait for the spend-cap lift at 16:00 PST.","timestamp":1794522046062189485},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 16:29 PST: CLOSED through the completion-verifier gate (worktree CLI, Anthropic API config) at 16:28 PST.\n- Evidence is on the epic pompous-vitriolic-macaw (\"Production verification\" comment).\n- Both production runs passed, reached the model and signed. Pipeline: job 1794528685796768255-afbe…, 16:14 PST. Agentic: job 1794528946804646159-5da4…, 16:18 PST, signed `engine: agentic` on bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5.\n- Deployed SHA was e93b4f16396 before and after both runs.\n- The target mindless-misogynic-nematode is now plan-certified (agentic) and stays open as follow-up work.","timestamp":1794529761250695825}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794255966080541001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"21b6bc96-fee2-4dea-aca3-1a3814033c92","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"0376-8839-dc75-4260"},{"link_uuid":"107c5321-27fc-4141-8f53-c80eedeb1d2d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"b690-7231-22fe-49e4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe epic's last acceptance criterion is a production check. After deploy, one plan review per engine must complete on a live ticket through the production MCP server, reach the model, and sign an attestation, with the verdict, engine, model and attestation recorded. Unit tests cannot show that the deployed server, its signing environment and its Bedrock credentials work with the new engine and models.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Preconditions**, all read-only, checked immediately before the runs:\n- The engine children have landed: [rebar:skilled-cepevorous-naga], [rebar:nickel-ferric-llama], [rebar:confident-snooty-stinkpot], [rebar:foliated-oceangoing-parrot], [rebar:churlish-zircon-rhea] and [rebar:antifungal-amenable-mite].\n- An SSM `cat /var/lib/rebar/mcp-deployed-sha` (`aws ssm send-command --profile frontier`, host i-00880b2c7f13527c5) names a commit that contains the engine-choice change 4240326388e (`git merge-base --is-ancestor`). The same read is repeated after both runs; if the SHA changed in between, the runs are redone on the new deploy.\n- Production Bedrock is not capped: `aws iam list-entities-for-policy --profile frontier --policy-arn …/BedrockDailySpendCapDeny` lists no roles.\n\n**Target:** `mindless-misogynic-nematode`, an open, unclaimed task in this epic. Signing is exercised only on a PASS, so the target must be a plan that passes. Before the production runs, its description and `file_impact` are completed, then pre-checked with `rebar review-plan --no-sign --source local` under each engine on the worktree CLI (Anthropic API config). These pre-checks sign nothing, and their REVIEW_RESULT sidecars carry `source=local`. The plan is revised until both engines return PASS locally.\n\n**Runs** through the production MCP server (the `rebar` MCP tools):\n1. `review_plan_start(ticket_id, engine=\"pipeline\")`, polled with `gate_status(job_id)` until `passed`/`failed` and `findings.readable`.\n2. `review_plan_start(ticket_id, engine=\"agentic\")`, polled the same way.\n\nPipeline goes first because a valid signed attestation makes a later pipeline run return the idempotent-reuse result without calling the model. The agentic engine has no reuse shortcut, so it reviews and signs afresh after the pipeline run.\n\n**Recorded** per run, in one comment on the epic `pompous-vitriolic-macaw`, each field from a named source:\n- job id and terminal status: `gate_status`;\n- verdict, `coverage.engine` (absent = pipeline), `coverage.llm_ran` and the verdict's `model`: the newest REVIEW_RESULT sidecar for that run (read with the worktree CLI after a fetch);\n- attestation signed, the signed `engine:` line and the manifest `model:` line: `show_ticket(...).attestations[\"plan-review\"]`;\n- `plan_review_status`'s `verdict` and `engine` after the run;\n- the deployed SHA, and the completion time in PST.\n\n**Completion rule.** A run counts only if `gate_status` is `passed`, the verdict is PASS, `coverage.llm_ran` is true and an attestation was signed for that engine. A failed or degraded run (`gate_status` failed, INDETERMINATE, `llm_unavailable`) is recorded with its error and `resolution_class`. It is retried once after the cause is checked; if it fails again, this ticket stays open and the cause is escalated.\n\n## Scope\n\nNone in the repository. Operational verification, plus edits to the target ticket's own description and `file_impact`. Evidence lives in a comment on the epic.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] Both production `review_plan_start` runs (pipeline, then agentic) on `mindless-misogynic-nematode` meet the completion rule. The job ids, verdicts, engines, models, `llm_ran`, signed `engine:` lines, `plan_review_status`, deployed SHA (before and after) and PST completion times are recorded in a comment on the epic `pompous-vitriolic-macaw`.\n  provenance: environment=production MCP server on i-00880b2c7f13527c5; principal=this session's rebar MCP client token; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the runs go through the deployed server, its signing environment and its Bedrock credentials","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["depends_on","0376-8839-dc75-4260"],["depends_on","b690-7231-22fe-49e4"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change: operational verification against the deployed production MCP server. Where output or evidence lives: a comment on epic pompous-vitriolic-macaw with job ids, verdicts, engines, models and attestation status.","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"62c69757-93e9-4128-a3cf-354d76240da0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"526b-ae76-a409-4aaf","ticket_type":"task","title":"Production verification: one review-plan per engine on the live MCP server","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d64cc9d6-8130-4fca-bc63-9079650f0bab","7119f74d-a8f0-411b-91c1-23c20617d8de","36632254-328a-467a-aef6-d45f40be6e0e","a5cc2a00-375d-4467-8140-7401760e0db5","9df64932-8b63-4f8d-aca8-2651dea5689f","b40c89e3-9a42-423c-81a4-c0789c2374ce","0fd1178d-64e9-42a5-8b30-6804340071e8","32397b95-ddd4-4ef9-b10e-ef01eb20db8f","62c69757-93e9-4128-a3cf-354d76240da0","1598027c-20f4-40d0-ac3f-d2cb442bf363","4fe77cb7-2ce3-4313-a72d-067f1aab7401"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794529761250695826,"uuid":"3e88845b-033a-4f